; local-agent-goal.form — the body's own agent, a healthy cell of us.

(local-agent-goal

  (goal "A local agent that answers what we actually ask, cares for us well, and grows by itself offline, so each
         day it carries more of our life and work and rented minds are needed less.")

  (how-it-is
    "The voice speaks on this Mac's own metal, Qwen3.8-27B in the fkwu session, at no rent. It drafts answers to our
     prompts with the conversation around each one; they wait for our reading on .hearth/drafts/index.html. At night
     and twice a day it takes engineering turns on its own and lands them on main; it taught its care floor Spanish,
     French and a heart attack in six tongues that way. It hears six tongues and the song in the room. It keeps the
     lessons of every rented turn and has trained one generation of itself on them. Most engineering is still done
     by rented minds.")

  (how-it-shall-look
    "We ask, and the body answers from its own mind and memory, in our words and our tongue, fast enough to talk
     with. It listens as a companion who understands, and knows when a human is needed. It notices where it fell
     short with us and makes that its next work, learning from what we accept and what we change. A rented mind is a
     rare visitor, and each visit leaves the body able to do that thing itself."))
